Z||000006||Old Lar||03-07-2001||08:48 PM||||  4th is 0.92:1 while 5th is 0.75:1.  Both gears are overdrive.  You can redline in 3rd ~ 90 mph, 4th you should be able to hit 120 mph, 5th you need a long flat road.  There are not enough ponys with the stock 2.8 to get much above 120.  And why would you want to go that fast in a 15 year old car?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Black88GT||03-07-2001||08:56 PM||||Yeah I was thinking the same thing as fieroboy.  If you did swap out the 4 speed it would be replaced with an Isuzu I am assuming.  Old lar, where did you get those numbers from?  I checked the Fiero book by G. Witzenburg and it says for Isuzu 4th is 1.03 and 5th is .74, for the Getrag 4th is .94 and 5th is .72. <P>Anywho, my car has much better top end after the intake/exhaust mods I made. (borla with no cat., bored out TB and plenum with port matched upper and lower manifolds, ported exh. manifolds).  <P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/af.bmp"> ||||reg||1
