Z||000019||Will||03-07-2001||10:27 PM||||The phenomenon you're experiencing comes from having a small V6 with a narrow power band low in the RPM range. I've noticed it on several Fieros I've driven. It can be remedied by installing a 3.4L TDC V6 or a Cadillac Northstar V8.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Or you could talk to this guy I've heard of.. his name is Chris West. I've heard he has some items that will assist you in getting that top end you are looking for. Check him out (well, his website anyway) - <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Will (edited 03-07-2001).]||||reg||1
